# The build context is the whole repo, but the image needs `server/` and nothing else:
# server/ imports only stdlib, fastapi, pydantic and starlette — never the `loom` client
# package. Everything excluded here is excluded because it has no runtime role, and this
# file is also AC5's first line of defence, so the two jobs are kept visibly separate.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trees the server does not need at runtime
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.github
client
test
docs
prompts
contract
server/tests

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artefacts and caches — rebuilt inside the image, never copied into it
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv
venv
build
dist
**/*.egg-info
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AC5: nothing secret-shaped may reach a layer
#
# The pilot database and the revisor token live OUTSIDE the repo (~/.loom-server/), so
# these patterns are not covering a known leak — they exist so that a stray copy made
# inside the tree cannot become one. `**/` is load-bearing: a bare `*.db` is anchored at
# the context root and would happily ship `some/dir/loom.db`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/revisor-token.txt
**/*.log
# The rest of wave m's SECRET_SHAPED list. None of these exist in the tree today; they are
# here so that the .dockerignore is a STRUCTURAL guard rather than one that happens to pass
# because nothing matched on the day CI ran.
**/credentials.json
**/.credentials.json
**/.netrc
**/id_rsa
**/id_ed25519
